// W5-11 U10b, R-399 (spec §18.1): an attribute starts an item when it starts with `@` or with the `#[` of
// another language; a `#` that no `[` follows is no item start, so the line of it is in the run of tokens
// of no item before it, which a line of `pub` alone starts, and that run is one unit with one error. The
// declaration after it is read: its use has no E0302.
pub                                                 //~ E0002 @4
#
fn ok() -> I32 { 1 }
fn calls() -> I32 {
  ok()
}
